{
  "id": "RAW_3451bb2ae3",
  "title": "Supabase 发布 Evals：一个开源基准测试，对 Claude Code、Codex 和 OpenCode 在真实 Supabase 任务上的表现进行评分",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/08/01/supabase-releases-evals-an-open-source-benchmark-that-scores-claude-code-codex-and-opencode-on-real-supabase-tasks/",
  "date": "2026-08-01 17:52:51",
  "author": "Michal Sutter",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Supabase has <a href=\"https://supabase.com/blog/introducing-supabase-evals\">open sourced Supabase Evals</a>, its benchmark and framework for testing how well AI agents build using Supabase. It runs coding agents including <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code\">Claude Code</a>, Codex, and <a href=\"https://opencode.ai/\">OpenCode</a> against real tasks, such as building a schema, debugging a failed <a href=\"https://supabase.com/edge-functions\">Edge Function</a>, or fixing a broken RLS policy, then scores the result. It powers the public leaderboard at <a href=\"https://supabase.com/evals\">supabase.com/evals</a> and an internal regression suite monitored daily.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-is-it-deployable\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Is it deployable?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Yes, today. <a href=\"https://github.com/supabase/evals\"><code>supabase/evals</code></a> is public under Apache-2.0 and runs locally via <code>pnpm</code>.</p>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li><strong>Industries</strong>: Developer tooling, cloud infrastructure, data platforms, and regulated backends in fintech or healthcare, where an agent writing a wrong <a href=\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/postgres/row-level-security\">RLS</a> policy is a security incident.</li>\n   <li><strong>Applications</strong>: Regression-testing docs and skill edits, gating SDK releases, and comparing agent harnesses head to head.</li>\n   <li><strong>Constraints</strong>: Local-stack runs need a Docker daemon, provider API keys, and ports 54321–54329 free.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-the-harness-works\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How the harness works</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Supabase defined three dimensions: <strong>products</strong> (database, auth, storage, edge-functions, realtime, cron, queues, vectors, data-api), <strong>topics</strong> (RLS, security, migrations, SQL, SDK, observability, self-hosting, tests, declarative-schema), and <strong>stages</strong> (build, deploy, investigate, resolve). It then picked the smallest scenario set touching each dimension once, grounded in support tickets, bug reports, and GitHub issues.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Scenarios split into two suites. <strong>Benchmark</strong> scenarios cover breadth and are published. <strong>Regression</strong> scenarios cover known failure modes, refresh daily, and do not move published scores.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every scenario runs against a real environment. The framework boots a hosted-like stack and a local CLI project in containers, so agents call the actual <a href=\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/mcp\">MCP server</a> and CLI. A <code>platform-lite</code> runtime exposes a Management API-compatible surface backed by <a href=\"https://github.com/supabase/supabase-lite\"><code>@supabase/lite</code></a>. Scoring combines deterministic checks with LLM-as-a-judge. Agents get one retry before grading.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Each eval directory holds <code>PROMPT.md</code> (task plus frontmatter), <code>EVAL.ts</code> (the scorer), and optional <code>remote/</code> and <code>local/</code> starting states. Shipping a <code>local/</code> workspace, or declaring <code>interface: cli</code>, boots a Docker sandbox with the real CLI installed.</p>\n  <!-- Marktechpost interactive embed: Supabase Evals explainer. Paste into a WordPress Custom HTML block. -->\n  <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"mtp-supabase-evals\" title=\"How Supabase Evals grades an AI coding agent\" loading=\"lazy\" scrolling=\"no\" srcdoc=\"&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\nbody{background:#121212;color:#ededed;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;padding:18px;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}\n.wrap{max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-radius:14px;background:#1a1a1a;overflow:hidden}\n.hd{padding:18px 20px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #2a2a2a;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#1e1e1e,#171717)}\n.eyebrow{font:600 10px/1 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.16em;color:#3ECF8E;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:9px}\n.hd h2{font-size:clamp(17px,3.1vw,21px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin-bottom:6px}\n.hd p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#a1a1a1}\n.tabs{display:flex;gap:6px;padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #2a2a2a;background:#161616;overflow-x:auto}\n.tab{flex:0 0 auto;padding:8px 14px;border:1px solid #2f2f2f;border-radius:999px;background:#1c1c1c;color:#9a9a9a;font:600 12px/1 inherit;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;transition:.18s}\n.tab:hover{color:#ededed;border-color:#3f3f3f}\n.tab.on{background:rgba(62,207,142,.13);border-color:#3ECF8E;color:#3ECF8E}\n.pane{display:none;padding:20px}\n.pane.on{display:block;animation:fade .3s ease}\n@keyframes fade{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(6px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n.hint{font:500 11px/1.5 inherit;color:#777;margin-bottom:14px}\n.hint b{color:#3ECF8E}\n\n/* pipeline */\n.flow{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:8px;overflow-x:auto;padding-bottom:6px}\n.node{flex:1 1 0;min-width:104px;border:1px solid #2f2f2f;border-radius:11px;background:#1c1c1c;padding:12px 10px;cursor:pointer;text-align:center;transition:.2s;position:relative}\n.node:hover{border-color:#3f3f3f;transform:translateY(-2px)}\n.node.on{border-color:#3ECF8E;background:rgba(62,207,142,.09);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(62,207,142,.28)}\n.node.lit{border-color:rgba(62,207,142,.65)}\n.nnum{font:700 9px/1 ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:#666;letter-spacing:.1em;margin-bottom:7px}\n.node.on .nnum{color:#3ECF8E}\n.nico{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:6px;line-height:1}\n.nlab{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.35}\n.node .dot{position:absolute;top:-4px;right:-4px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:#3ECF8E;opacity:0;transition:.2s}\n.node.lit .dot{opacity:1;animation:pulse 1s infinite}\n@keyframes pulse{0%,100%{transform:scale(1);opacity:1}50%{transform:scale(1.6);opacity:.45}}\n.detail{margin-top:14px;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-left:2px solid #3ECF8E;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;background:#171717;padding:14px 16px;min-height:96px}\n.detail h4{font-size:13px;color:#3ECF8E;margin-bottom:7px;font-weight:700}\n.detail p{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.65;color:#bdbdbd}\n.detail code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;background:#242424;color:#3ECF8E;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px}\n.btn{margin-top:13px;padding:8px 15px;border:1px solid #3ECF8E;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(62,207,142,.1);color:#3ECF8E;font:600 12px/1 inherit;cursor:pointer;transition:.18s}\n.btn:hover{background:rgba(62,207,142,.2)}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:default}\n\n/* anatomy */\n.tree{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px}\n.f{border:1px solid #2f2f2f;border-radius:10px;background:#1c1c1c;padding:11px 13px;cursor:pointer;transition:.18s}\n.f:hover{border-color:#3f3f3f}\n.f.on{border-color:#3ECF8E;background:rgba(62,207,142,.09)}\n.f .fn{font:600 12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:#3ECF8E;margin-bottom:4px}\n.f .fd{font-size:11px;color:#8d8d8d;line-height:1.45}\n\n/* runtimes */\n.tog{display:flex;gap:6px;margin-bottom:14px;background:#161616;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-radius:10px;padding:4px;width:fit-content}\n.tg{padding:8px 16px;border-radius:7px;background:transparent;border:0;color:#8d8d8d;font:600 12px/1 inherit;cursor:pointer;transition:.18s}\n.tg.on{background:rgba(62,207,142,.15);color:#3ECF8E}\n.lanes{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px}\n.lane{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-radius:10px;background:#1c1c1c;padding:11px 13px;opacity:.28;transition:.35s;transform:translateX(-6px)}\n.lane.act{opacity:1;transform:none;border-color:rgba(62,207,142,.45)}\n.lane .lb{font:600 10px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:#3ECF8E;background:rgba(62,207,142,.12);border:1px solid rgba(62,207,142,.3);padding:4px 8px;border-radius:6px;flex:0 0 auto}\n.lane .lt{font-size:12px;color:#bdbdbd;line-height:1.5}\n\n/* findings */\n.rows{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:112px 1fr 46px;align-items:center;gap:10px}\n.rn{font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;color:#cfcfcf}\n.track{height:20px;background:#202020;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden}\n.bar{height:100%;width:0;border-radius:6px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#2a9d6e,#3ECF8E);transition:width .85s cubic-bezier(.34,1.2,.5,1)}\n.rv{font:700 12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;color:#3ECF8E;text-align:right}\n.note{margin-top:14px;font-size:11.5px;color:#8d8d8d;line-height:1.6;border-top:1px solid #262626;padding-top:11px}\n.note b{color:#cfcfcf}\n.ft{padding:11px 20px;border-top:1px solid #2a2a2a;background:#161616;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:11px;color:#6d6d6d}\n.ft b{color:#3ECF8E}\n.ft a{color:#8d8d8d;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid #333}\n.ft a:hover{color:#3ECF8E}\n@media(max-width:640px){\n body{padding:10px}.pane{padding:15px}.tree{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n .row{grid-template-columns:88px 1fr 42px;gap:7px}.rn{font-size:10.5px}\n .node{min-width:92px}.lane{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}\n}\n&lt;/style&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;wrap&quot;&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;hd&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;eyebrow&quot;&gt;Interactive Explainer&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;How Supabase Evals grades an AI coding agent&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;Every scenario runs against a real Supabase environment. Click through the pipeline, the eval file layout, the two runtimes, and the published Build-stage results.&lt;/p&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;tabs&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab on&quot; data-p=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Run pipeline&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Eval anatomy&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;Two runtimes&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Build-stage results&lt;/button&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;!-- PIPELINE --&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;pane on&quot; id=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;hint&quot;&gt;Click any stage — or press &lt;b&gt;Run the pipeline&lt;/b&gt; to watch a scenario flow end to end.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;flow&quot; id=&quot;flow&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;detail&quot; id=&quot;det&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; id=&quot;run&quot;&gt;▶ Run the pipeline&lt;/button&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;!-- ANATOMY --&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;pane&quot; id=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;hint&quot;&gt;Every eval lives at &lt;b&gt;evals/&amp;lt;id&amp;gt;/&lt;/b&gt;. Click a file to see what it holds.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;tree&quot; id=&quot;tree&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;detail&quot; id=&quot;det2&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;!-- RUNTIMES --&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;pane&quot; id=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;hint&quot;&gt;The harness picks a runtime &lt;b&gt;automatically&lt;/b&gt;, per eval. Toggle to compare.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;tog&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;button class=&quot;tg on&quot; data-r=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Tools evals&lt;/button&gt;\n   &lt;button class=&quot;tg&quot; data-r=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Local-stack evals&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;lanes&quot; id=&quot;lanes&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;note&quot; id=&quot;rnote&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;!-- FINDINGS --&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;pane&quot; id=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;hint&quot;&gt;Published &lt;b&gt;Build stage&lt;/b&gt; pass rates. Toggle the Supabase agent skill on and off.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;tog&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;button class=&quot;tg&quot; data-s=&quot;0&quot;&gt;No skill loaded&lt;/button&gt;\n   &lt;button class=&quot;tg on&quot; data-s=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Skill loaded&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;rows&quot; id=&quot;rows&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;b&gt;Also measured:&lt;/b&gt; Codex / GPT-5.6 reads about 8 docs pages per scenario, versus roughly 2 for Claude Code, which checks the docs in under 40% of scenarios even with skills loaded. Rewriting the Postgres best-practices skill description lifted its activation from about 1 in 10 sessions to 60%.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;\n   Figures are a snapshot from Supabase's launch post (31 Jul 2026). Results move as models change — check the live page.\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;ft&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;span&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&quot;https://supabase.com/blog/introducing-supabase-evals&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Supabase blog&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/supabase/evals&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;supabase/evals&lt;/a&gt; · Apache-2.0&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;Marktechpost&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\nvar STAGES=[\n {i:&quot;📝&quot;,l:&quot;Scenario&quot;,h:&quot;1 · A real scenario&quot;,t:&quot;Each eval is grounded in a real problem — a support ticket, bug report, or GitHub issue. &lt;code&gt;PROMPT.md&lt;/code&gt; carries the task the agent sees plus frontmatter tagging its stage, product, and topic.&quot;},\n {i:&quot;🐳&quot;,l:&quot;Environments&quot;,h:&quot;2 · Two real environments&quot;,t:&quot;The framework boots a hosted-like Supabase stack and a local CLI project in containers. &lt;code&gt;platform-lite&lt;/code&gt; serves a Management API-compatible surface backed by &lt;code&gt;@supabase/lite&lt;/code&gt;.&quot;},\n {i:&quot;🤖&quot;,l:&quot;Agent runs&quot;,h:&quot;3 · The agent works&quot;,t:&quot;Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, or an AI SDK agent invokes the real Supabase MCP server and CLI — not mocks. Skills load lazily: only name and description sit in the system prompt.&quot;},\n {i:&quot;🔁&quot;,l:&quot;One retry&quot;,h:&quot;4 · One retry allowed&quot;,t:&quot;To cut false negatives while keeping runs sustainable, agents may retry once after a failure before they are graded.&quot;},\n {i:&quot;⚖️&quot;,l:&quot;Scoring&quot;,h:&quot;5 · Deterministic + judge&quot;,t:&quot;&lt;code&gt;EVAL.ts&lt;/code&gt; exports the scorer. Deterministic checks confirm things like whether a user can reach certain data or an Edge Function returns the expected result; an LLM judge handles semantic calls.&quot;},\n {i:&quot;📊&quot;,l:&quot;Results&quot;,h:&quot;6 · Benchmark or regression&quot;,t:&quot;Benchmark scenarios go to the public site and run when assessing new changes or harnesses. Regression scenarios track known failure modes and refresh daily, without moving published scores.&quot;}\n];\nvar FILES=[\n {n:&quot;PROMPT.md&quot;,d:&quot;Task + frontmatter&quot;,h:&quot;PROMPT.md&quot;,t:&quot;Frontmatter plus the task description the agent sees. Keys drive discovery and the site filters: &lt;code&gt;stage&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;suite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;product&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;topic&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;motivation&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;suite&lt;/code&gt; is required on every eval.&quot;},\n {n:&quot;EVAL.ts&quot;,d:&quot;The scorer&quot;,h:&quot;EVAL.ts&quot;,t:&quot;A default-exported scorer. Scorers check what the agent produced, never what the harness provisioned — with &lt;code&gt;projectRunning: true&lt;/code&gt;, only the agent's deltas are scored.&quot;},\n {n:&quot;remote/&quot;,d:&quot;Hosted project state&quot;,h:&quot;remote/ — optional&quot;,t:&quot;The hosted project's starting state, seeded into platform-lite: &lt;code&gt;project.sql&lt;/code&gt; for the database, &lt;code&gt;logs.jsonl&lt;/code&gt; for observability logs, and &lt;code&gt;functions/&lt;/code&gt; for already-deployed Edge Functions.&quot;},\n {n:&quot;local/&quot;,d:&quot;Agent workspace&quot;,h:&quot;local/ — optional&quot;,t:&quot;The developer's working directory, copied into the sandbox before the agent starts. Its presence is also a runtime switch: ship a &lt;code&gt;local/&lt;/code&gt; and the eval boots a Docker sandbox.&quot;}\n];\nvar RUN=[\n {lanes:[[&quot;PROMPT&quot;,&quot;Agent gets the task, with no local/ directory and no interface: cli&quot;],[&quot;TOOLS&quot;,&quot;It works through the experiment's MCP / tool surface only — there is no filesystem&quot;],[&quot;SKILLS&quot;,&quot;A load_skill tool returns a skill's full instructions on demand&quot;],[&quot;SCORE&quot;,&quot;The resulting project state or report is graded&quot;]],\n  note:&quot;&lt;b&gt;Tools evals&lt;/b&gt; exercise the MCP surface in isolation. Because the agent has no filesystem, skills are fetched through a tool call rather than read from disk.&quot;},\n {lanes:[[&quot;PROMPT&quot;,&quot;Eval ships a local/ workspace or declares interface: cli&quot;],[&quot;SANDBOX&quot;,&quot;A fresh Docker container boots per attempt, with the real Supabase CLI installed&quot;],[&quot;STACK&quot;,&quot;The agent runs supabase init / start / db / test against a live local stack&quot;],[&quot;EXPORT&quot;,&quot;The workspace is copied back to the host so scorers run vite / vitest against it&quot;]],\n  note:&quot;&lt;b&gt;Local-stack evals&lt;/b&gt; need a running Docker daemon, and default ports 54321–54329 free. A &lt;code&gt;services:&lt;/code&gt; list keeps stack boots fast by starting only what the scenario needs.&quot;}\n];\nvar SCORES=[\n {n:&quot;Opus 5&quot;,off:100,on:100},\n {n:&quot;Kimi K3&quot;,off:100,on:100},\n {n:&quot;GPT-5.6 Sol&quot;,off:89,on:100},\n {n:&quot;Sonnet 5&quot;,off:78,on:100},\n {n:&quot;GPT-5.4 mini&quot;,off:78,on:89}\n];\n\nfunction $(s){return document.querySelector(s)}\nfunction all(s){return [].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll(s))}\n\n/* tabs */\nall('.tab').forEach(function(b){b.onclick=function(){\n all('.tab').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n all('.pane').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n b.classList.add('on');$('#'+b.dataset.p).classList.add('on');\n}});\n\n/* pipeline */\nvar flow=$('#flow');\nSTAGES.forEach(function(s,i){\n var d=document.createElement('div');d.className='node';d.dataset.i=i;\n d.innerHTML='&lt;span class=&quot;dot&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;nnum&quot;&gt;0'+(i+1)+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;nico&quot;&gt;'+s.i+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;nlab&quot;&gt;'+s.l+'&lt;/div&gt;';\n d.onclick=function(){pick(i)};flow.appendChild(d);\n});\nfunction pick(i){\n all('#flow .node').forEach(function(n,j){n.classList.toggle('on',j===i)});\n $('#det').innerHTML='&lt;h4&gt;'+STAGES[i].h+'&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;'+STAGES[i].t+'&lt;/p&gt;';\n}\npick(0);\nvar busy=false;\n$('#run').onclick=function(){\n if(busy)return;busy=true;this.disabled=true;\n var nodes=all('#flow .node');nodes.forEach(function(n){n.classList.remove('lit')});\n var i=0;var t=setInterval(function(){\n  if(i&gt;0)nodes[i-1].classList.remove('lit');\n  if(i&gt;=nodes.length){clearInterval(t);busy=false;$('#run').disabled=false;return}\n  nodes[i].classList.add('lit');pick(i);i++;\n },900);\n};\n\n/* anatomy */\nvar tree=$('#tree');\nFILES.forEach(function(f,i){\n var d=document.createElement('div');d.className='f';\n d.innerHTML='&lt;div class=&quot;fn&quot;&gt;'+f.n+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;fd&quot;&gt;'+f.d+'&lt;/div&gt;';\n d.onclick=function(){\n  all('#tree .f').forEach(function(x,j){x.classList.toggle('on',j===i)});\n  $('#det2').innerHTML='&lt;h4&gt;'+f.h+'&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;'+f.t+'&lt;/p&gt;';\n };\n tree.appendChild(d);\n});\nall('#tree .f')[0].click();\n\n/* runtimes */\nfunction drawRun(k){\n var L=$('#lanes');L.innerHTML='';\n RUN[k].lanes.forEach(function(x,i){\n  var d=document.createElement('div');d.className='lane';\n  d.innerHTML='&lt;span class=&quot;lb&quot;&gt;'+x[0]+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;lt&quot;&gt;'+x[1]+'&lt;/span&gt;';\n  L.appendChild(d);setTimeout(function(){d.classList.add('act')},120*i+60);\n });\n $('#rnote').innerHTML=RUN[k].note;\n}\nall('[data-r]').forEach(function(b){b.onclick=function(){\n all('[data-r]').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n b.classList.add('on');drawRun(+b.dataset.r);\n}});\ndrawRun(0);\n\n/* findings */\nvar rows=$('#rows');\nSCORES.forEach(function(s){\n var d=document.createElement('div');d.className='row';\n d.innerHTML='&lt;div class=&quot;rn&quot;&gt;'+s.n+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;rv&quot;&gt;—&lt;/div&gt;';\n rows.appendChild(d);\n});\nfunction drawScores(on){\n all('#rows .row').forEach(function(r,i){\n  var v=on?SCORES[i].on:SCORES[i].off;\n  r.querySelector('.bar').style.width=v+'%';\n  r.querySelector('.rv').textContent=v+'%';\n });\n}\nall('[data-s]').forEach(function(b){b.onclick=function(){\n all('[data-s]').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n b.classList.add('on');drawScores(b.dataset.s==='1');\n}});\ndrawScores(true);\n\n/* auto-resize */\nfunction ping(){\n try{parent.postMessage({mtpEmbed:'supabase-evals',height:document.body.offsetHeight+40},'*')}catch(e){}\n}\nwindow.addEventListener('load',ping);\nsetInterval(ping,400);\ndocument.addEventListener('click',function(){setTimeout(ping,60)});\n&lt;/script&gt;\n\"></iframe>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-findings\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Findings</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Agents pass most scenarios with no skill loaded. In the Build stage, Opus 5 and Kimi K3 both scored 100% unaided. Skills closed the rest of the gap: Sonnet 5 rose from 78% to 100%, GPT-5.6 Sol from 89% to 100%, and GPT-5.4 mini from 78% to 89%.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Three weaknesses surfaced. Agents hand-write migrations instead of using <a href=\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/local-development/declarative-database-schemas\">declarative schemas</a>, prompting a <a href=\"https://github.com/supabase/agent-skills/pull/120\">skill guidance update</a>. Agents verify auth by hand rather than reaching for <a href=\"https://supabase.com/blog/introducing-supabase-server\"><code>@supabase/server</code></a>, prompting a <a href=\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth/choosing-a-server-package\">package selection guide</a>. And docs usage varies sharply: Codex / GPT-5.6 reads roughly 8 docs pages per scenario versus about 2 for Claude Code, which checks docs in under 40% of scenarios even with skills loaded.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>Supabase open sourced <code>supabase/evals</code> under Apache-2.0.</li>\n   <li>Scenarios run against real containerized Supabase stacks, not mocks.</li>\n   <li>Scoring mixes deterministic checks with LLM-as-a-judge; one retry allowed.</li>\n   <li>Skills mattered least for top models, most for smaller ones.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the<strong>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://supabase.com/blog/introducing-supabase-evals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical details</a> </strong>and <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/supabase/evals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GitHub Repo</a>.&nbsp;</strong>Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.aidevsignals.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://forms.gle/wbash1wF6efRj8G58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.9 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <div class=\"m-a-box \" data-box-layout=\"slim\" data-box-position=\"below\" data-multiauthor=\"false\" data-author-id=\"676\" data-author-type=\"user\" data-author-archived=\"\">\n   <div class=\"m-a-box-container\">\n    <div class=\"m-a-box-tab m-a-box-content m-a-box-profile\" data-profile-layout=\"layout-1\" data-author-ref=\"user-676\" itemscope itemid=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/michal-sutter/\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Person\">\n     <div class=\"m-a-box-content-middle\">\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-avatar\" data-source=\"local\">\n       <a class=\"m-a-box-avatar-url\" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/michal-sutter/\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-150x150.png\" class=\"attachment-150x150 size-150x150\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" srcset=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-150x150.png 150w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-70x70.png 70w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-24x24.png 24w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-48x48.png 48w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-96x96.png 96w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" data-attachment-id=\"72715\" data-permalink=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0r9sv6nw5xk-zkphw_uarv5vw1st6oslnlunovwg/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg.png\" data-orig-size=\"832,960\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/a-professional-linkedin-headshot-photogr_0jcmb0R9Sv6nW5XK-zkPHw_uARV5VW1ST6osLNlunoVWg.png\"></a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-data\">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-name\">\n        <h5 itemprop=\"name\"><a class=\"m-a-box-name-url \" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/michal-sutter/\" itemprop=\"url\"> Michal Sutter</a></h5>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-meta\">\n        <a href=\"#\" class=\"m-a-box-data-toggle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-more-posts\">+ posts</span></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-bio\" itemprop=\"description\">\n        <p>Michal Sutter is a data science professional with a Master of Science in Data Science from the University of Padova. With a solid foundation in statistical analysis, machine learning, and data engineering, Michal excels at transforming complex datasets into actionable insights.</p>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-related\" data-related-layout=\"layout-1\"></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "Supabase 开源了 Evals，这是一个开源基准测试框架，通过容器化环境和混合评分，评估 Claude Code、Codex、OpenCode 等 AI 编程智能体在真实 Supabase 任务上的表现。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "Supabase 开源了 Evals，这是一个开源基准测试框架，通过容器化环境和混合评分，评估 Claude Code、Codex、OpenCode 等 AI 编程智能体在真实 Supabase 任务上的表现。",
  "summary": "本文介绍了 Supabase Evals，一个开源基准测试框架，用于测试 AI 智能体执行真实 Supabase 任务的能力，例如构建 schema、调试 Edge Functions 和修复 RLS 策略。该框架使用包含实际 MCP 服务器和 CLI 工具的容器化环境，将确定性检查与基于 LLM 的评判相结合。主要发现表明，Opus 5 和 Kimi K3 等顶级模型在构建阶段的无辅助得分达到 100%，而技能显著提升了较小模型的性能。该系统揭示了三个主要弱点：手动迁移实践、认证验证方法以及各智能体在文档使用上的不一致。Evals 以 Apache-2.0 许可发布，为公开排行榜和内部回归测试提供支持，并每日更新。",
